description: Ban hardcoded business content, mocks, and magic values in production
alwaysApply: true
---

# No hardcoding / no production mocks

## Forbidden in production code

- Hardcoded customer copy, prices, discounts, capacities, durations, locations, URLs, currencies, roles, statuses, locale lists, or business rules
- Magic strings/numbers in production logic (centralize true technical constants as named typed values)
- Fake reviews, ratings, bookings, placeholder arrays, static JSON content, or runtime fixtures
- Using Storage buckets as a content database

## Required sources

- Business and editorial content → database via typed backend contracts
- Secrets and environment-specific values → validated env vars (`src/lib/env`)
- Empty DB states → real empty UI (never fabricate inventory)

## Tests only

Test fixtures may live only in test code and must never be imported by production modules.
